midation and mitochondrial translation. Located in mitochondrion. Part of glutamyl-tRNA(Gln) amidotransferase complex. Implicated in combined oxidative phosphorylation deficiency 40. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9H0R6","text":"Catalytic subunit of the mitochondrial Glu-tRNA(Gln) amidotransferase complex GatCAB (Probable) (PubMed:19805282). GatCAB allows the formation of correctly charged Gln-tRNA(Gln) through the transamidation of misacylated Glu-tRNA(Gln) in the mitochondria. The reaction takes place in the presence of glutamine and ATP through an activated gamma-phospho-Glu-tRNA(Gln) (By similarity). This subunit probably catalyzes the hydrolysis of the amido donor Gln, releasing ammonia that is sequestered within a channel in the GatCAB complex and made available to subunit B for downstream aminolysis of Glu-tRNA(Gln) (Probable). Required for the stability of GATB (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}